WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.920
It was the final round of King Henry's archery contest.

2
00:00:05.921 --> 00:00:09.659
The Bishop of Hereford sat next to the queen.

3
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.908
The king's page led three men onto the field.

4
00:00:12.909 --> 00:00:16.238
They were named Gilbert, Tepus, and Hubert.

5
00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:20.105
They bowed to the king and queen.

6
00:00:20.106 --> 00:00:23.516
The queen's page led three men onto the field.

7
00:00:23.517 --> 00:00:27.969
They were Robin Hood, Little John, and Will Scarlet.

8
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:38.052
When the queen's archers bowed, the Bishop of Hereford looked startled, as if he'd just been stung by a wasp.

9
00:00:38.053 --> 00:00:42.563
"I know those men!" he shouted in surprise. "They're—"

10
00:00:42.564 --> 00:00:49.333
"Robert of Locksley and his friends," the queen said with a smile.

11
00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.991
Robin used this name when he was in disguise.

12
00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:57.942
The bishop's face was red with anger, but he didn't say anything more.

13
00:00:57.943 --> 00:01:00.864
"Locksley!" the queen called to Robin.

14
00:01:00.865 --> 00:01:03.298
"I've made a bet with the king.

15
00:01:03.299 --> 00:01:08.167
I told him that you and your men can outshoot any of his men.

16
00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:13.003
I hope, for my sake, that I'm not wrong."

17
00:01:13.004 --> 00:01:16.656
"We'll do our best for you!" said Robin.

18
00:01:16.657 --> 00:01:20.956
Little John shifted his feet, looking a little shy.

19
00:01:20.957 --> 00:01:24.761
"You're so lovely, Queen Eleanor," he said.

20
00:01:24.762 --> 00:01:28.168
"Is there anyone who wouldn't do their best for you?"

21
00:01:28.169 --> 00:01:30.769
The queen laughed.

22
00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:33.767
But the bishop didn't crack a smile.

23
00:01:33.768 --> 00:01:35.783
And neither did King Henry.

24
00:01:35.784 --> 00:01:39.390
He was glaring at his wife.

25
00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:43.599
"Who are these men?" the king demanded.

26
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.620
Before the queen could speak, the bishop leaped to his feet.

27
00:01:47.621 --> 00:01:52.109
"Locksley is really the outlaw Robin Hood!" he burst out.

28
00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:57.970
"That giant fellow is called Little John, and the other one is Will Scarlet.

29
00:01:57.971 --> 00:02:00.633
They both belong to Robin Hood's band.

30
00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:05.104
All three of them are robbers and thieves."

31
00:02:05.105 --> 00:02:11.733
The king looked stunned. "Is this true?" he asked the queen sternly.

32
00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:15.393
"Yes," the queen replied, smiling.

33
00:02:15.394 --> 00:02:18.488
"The bishop knows these men well.

34
00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:24.050
He and some of his friars spent three days with them in Sherwood Forest.

35
00:02:24.051 --> 00:02:31.143
Remember, dear, you promised these archers would be safe for forty days."

36
00:02:31.144 --> 00:02:35.623
"I'll keep my promise." The king scowled.

37
00:02:35.624 --> 00:02:41.863
"But when those forty days are up, Robin Hood should beware.

38
00:02:41.864 --> 00:02:46.193
Things may not go exactly as he wants."

39
00:02:46.194 --> 00:02:49.084
He turned to Gilbert, Tepus, and Hubert.

40
00:02:49.085 --> 00:02:55.377
"If you beat Robin Hood and his men, I'll reward you well.

41
00:02:55.378 --> 00:03:00.645
Go now, and do your best."

42
00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:06.015
The men began to get ready, stringing their bows and carefully selecting their arrows.

43
00:03:06.016 --> 00:03:10.882
The match began. No one had ever seen such amazing shooting.

44
00:03:10.883 --> 00:03:14.626
Hubert went first, and made his best shots of the day.

45
00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.781
Will Scarlet went next.

46
00:03:16.782 --> 00:03:22.132
He shot too cautiously and couldn't beat Hubert.

47
00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:25.513
Little John easily beat Tepus.

48
00:03:25.514 --> 00:03:31.114
Gilbert tried his best and hit two bull's-eyes with his three arrows.

49
00:03:31.115 --> 00:03:35.591
"Well done, Gilbert!" Robin slapped him on the shoulder.

50
00:03:35.592 --> 00:03:38.770
"You really should come to Sherwood Forest."

51
00:03:38.771 --> 00:03:44.422
He picked up his bow, selected an arrow, and then instantly shot a bull's-eye.

52
00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:47.561
The crowd gasped.

53
00:03:47.562 --> 00:03:52.661
"There's nothing interesting to shoot here in London," Robin said to Gilbert.

54
00:03:52.662 --> 00:03:54.729
He shot another bull's-eye.

55
00:03:54.730 --> 00:04:02.819
"What do you think?" Robin hit another bull's-eye.

56
00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:07.165
A murmur went through the crowd and then everyone started clapping.

57
00:04:07.166 --> 00:04:09.707
Gilbert rushed to shake hands with Robin.

58
00:04:09.708 --> 00:04:13.805
"I think you're the best archer in the world!"

59
00:04:13.806 --> 00:04:16.292
King Henry wasn't so gracious.

60
00:04:16.293 --> 00:04:21.130
"It's time for us to go," he snapped at Queen Eleanor.

61
00:04:21.131 --> 00:04:26.731
They stood up and left the field, without watching the judges give Robin first prize.

62
00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:41.674
Robin won a trumpet, a purse of gold coins, and ten gold arrows.

63
00:04:41.675 --> 00:04:45.969
"I'll keep this silver trumpet," said Robin after the ceremony.

64
00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:49.039
"But, Gilbert, you shot the best of the king's men.

65
00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.806
So I am giving you the purse of gold coins."

66
00:04:52.807 --> 00:04:55.915
At this, the crowd cheered.

67
00:04:55.916 --> 00:05:00.143
"What will you do with the ten gold arrows?" asked Little John.

68
00:05:00.144 --> 00:05:04.039
"I'll give them to the top ten archers," replied Robin.

69
00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.735
Another loud cheer rose from the crowd.

70
00:05:07.736 --> 00:05:10.776
Robin handed out the arrows to the men.

71
00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:12.920
"Keep them to remember this day.

72
00:05:12.921 --> 00:05:15.715
It was an honor to compete against you."

73
00:05:15.716 --> 00:05:21.646
"Hooray!" cried the crowd. "Hooray for Robin!"

74
00:05:21.647 --> 00:05:25.989
The archers swarmed around Robin and his men, eager to meet them.

75
00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:28.899
Everyone was talking loudly.

76
00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:32.990
A member of the king's guard tapped Robin's shoulder.

77
00:05:32.991 --> 00:05:35.555
"I have a message for you," said the guard.

78
00:05:35.556 --> 00:05:39.878
"The queen's page said to tell you: The lion growls. Beware.

79
00:05:39.879 --> 00:05:42.038
Do you know what that means?"

80
00:05:42.039 --> 00:05:46.238
"Yes." Robin nodded. "Thank you for delivering this warning."

81
00:05:46.239 --> 00:05:51.832
He turned to his men. "Little John! Will! We must be going."

82
00:05:51.833 --> 00:05:56.143
As they hurried away, Robin explained the reason for their haste.

83
00:05:56.144 --> 00:05:58.834
"That was a message from the queen," he said.

84
00:05:58.835 --> 00:06:03.942
"King Henry is furious!"

